{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1776857376,"nonce":"KeCjuju5unWztlA8A1aB7mrYVOY=","title":"cmd_resume breaks on review session IDs","message":"## Summary\n\n`nightshift resume review-\u003cid\u003e` fails with \"No session state\" because `cmd_resume` passes the raw session ID to `launch.py` without:\n\n1. Using `resolve_session()` to resolve the full session ID\n2. Detecting review sessions (prefix `review-`) and adding `--step review`\n3. Stripping the `review-` prefix before passing to `_resolve_names()`\n\n## Root Cause\n\n`launch.py:_resolve_names()` does `short_id = issue_id[:SHORT_ID_LEN]` (12 chars).\nWhen you pass `review-47ca35f` (15 chars), it truncates to `review-47ca3` and looks for a non-existent session.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n```bash\nnightshift resume review-47ca35f\n# Error: No session state at .nightshift/sessions/review-47ca3\n```\n\n## Workaround\n\nUse bare issue ID with explicit flags:\n```bash\npython host/launch.py 47ca35f --resume --step review --workflow REVIEW.md\n```\n\n## Fix\n\nIn `host/cli.py:cmd_resume`:\n1. Use `resolve_session(a.issue_id)` to get full session ID\n2. Detect if session starts with `REVIEW_SESSION_PREFIX`\n3. If review: strip prefix, add `--step review`, use REVIEW.md workflow\n\n## Tests\n\n- tests/test_cli_commands.py::test_cmd_resume_review_session_strips_prefix\n- tests/test_cli_commands.py::test_cmd_resume_review_session_adds_step_flag\n\nREQ: REQ-031 (dual-agent workflow)","files":null}]}